Description: Implements the HERITAGE framework (Hierarchical Effects Regression
    with Interactions for Trait Analysis in GEnetics). HERITAGE reinterprets
    pedigrees as directed networks of intergenerational influence and decomposes
    each phenotype into (1) a direct effect of personal genotypes and (2) a
    kinship-weighted ancestral spillover reflecting genetic nurture. It enforces
    hierarchical sparsity: spillover effects are only allowed when the
    corresponding direct effect is non-zero. Estimation uses the Hierarchical
    Alternating Minimization Algorithm (HAMA). The package also provides
    utilities to compute kinship-weighted spillover covariates from pedigree
    data and a grid-search wrapper for joint hyperparameter selection.
